# RESOLVED 2026-09-07. The curated public snapshot is pushed and live. This is a
# SEPARATE repository from the private working one
# (sathvikloke/hne-tme-immune-specificity-audit), which stays private — its
# history carries the cluster host and username, home paths and a personal
# email, and no later fix would remove them from that history. Do not point
# this field at the private name.
repository-code: "https://github.com/sathvikloke/immune-specificity-index"
abstract: >-
  Analysis code for an audit of H&E-inferred tumor microenvironment
  signatures across 7,168 TCGA patients in 31 cancer types. Defines an
  immune-specificity index (ISI) that residualizes signatures on the
  within-cancer-type global expression axis and disattenuates for the
  reliability of the residualized score, and runs the identical
  random-gene-set null against progression-free interval.
keywords:
  - computational pathology
  - tumor microenvironment
  - gene signatures
  - reproducibility
  - foundation models
license: MIT
# `version` and `date-released` name the frozen analysis snapshot every quoted
# number comes from -- the annotated tag `prereg-2026-08-18`, which is the only
# tag in the author's PRIVATE working repository. The previous
# `date-released: "2026-08-19"` matched no tag, no release and no artifact; it
# was a date someone typed. If a public release is ever cut, both fields move to
# that release and not before.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE "FIXING" THE VERSION STRING. This file is published inside the
# public snapshot, and that snapshot is a fresh single-commit repository with
# ZERO tags -- verified 2026-09-07 with `git ls-remote --heads --tags`. So
# `version` below is a VERSION STRING that happens to be spelled like a tag; it
# is NOT a reference a reader can resolve there, and this comment used to say
# "the only tag in the repository", which read as a claim about whichever
# repository the reader was holding. Do not add a tag to the public snapshot to
# make this resolve: its only commit is dated 2026-09-07, so the tag would assert
# a timestamp that does not exist. The open decision is tracked in the private
# working repository (`16-YOUR-TASKS.md`), which is not part of this deposit.
version: "prereg-2026-08-18"
date-released: "2026-08-18"
